## Why This Question Is Asked
This question assesses the ability to design per-key rate-limiting state, implement TTL-based eviction, ensure idempotence across replays, and align with KCNA consumer semantics.

## Key Concepts
- Per-key sliding or fixed-window counters
- TTL-based eviction and memory safety
- Idempotence with replay handling
- Backpressure and stable commit boundaries

## Code Example
```javascript
class RateStore {
  constructor(ttlMs) {
    this.ttlMs = ttlMs;
    this.store = new Map();
  }
  get(key, minute) {
    return this.store.get(`${key}:${minute}`) ?? 0;
  }
  increment(key, minute) {
    const entry = this.store.get(`${key}:${minute}`) ?? { count: 0, timestamp: Date.now() };
    entry.count++;
    this.store.set(`${key}:${minute}`, entry);
    return entry.count;
  }
  prune() {
    const now = Date.now();
    for (const [key, entry] of this.store.entries()) {
      if (now - entry.timestamp > this.ttlMs) {
        this.store.delete(key);
      }
    }
  }
}

class AlertingSink {
  constructor(limit = 100, windowMs = 60000) {
    this.rateStore = new RateStore(windowMs);
    this.limit = limit;
    this.seenMessages = new Set();
  }
  onMessage(ctx, msg) {
    if (this.seenMessages.has(msg.offset)) return;
    this.seenMessages.add(msg.offset);

    const minute = Math.floor(Date.now() / 60000);
    const count = this.rateStore.increment(msg.key, minute);
    if (count <= this.limit) {
      ctx.emitAlert(msg);
    }
  }
  commitOffsets() {}
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests knowledge of per-tenant security, ACLs, and token lifecycles in KCNA. Assesses gateway/broker enforcement, rotation and revocation strategies, and robust auditing under multi-tenant pressure. Calls for practical test plans and rollback considerations.

## Key Concepts

- Per-tenant ACLs with topic-level granularity
- JWT/OAuth tokens and short-lived credentials
- Gateway and broker ACL enforcement and performance impact
- Rotation, revocation, and audit logging
- Observability and test strategies with edge cases

## Code Example

```javascript
// Implementation snippet: token + ACL check
function authorize(token, topic, operation) {
  const claims = decodeJWT(token);
  if (Date.now() >= claims.exp) return false;
  if (!claims.tenants.includes(claims.tenant)) return false;
  const acl = ACL_STORE[claims.tenant]?.[topic];
  if (!acl) return false;
  return acl.includes(operation);
}
```

