## Why This Is Asked

To test understanding of consumer rebalances and offset management, a common pitfall for beginners where duplicates occur if offsets aren't tracked during rebalances.

## Key Concepts

- Consumer group rebalancing
- Per-topic offset tracking
- In-flight state
- Safe commit on revoke
- Timeouts and fault tolerance

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo code showing API hooks
class RebalanceSafeConsumer {
  constructor() { this.committedOffsets = new Map(); this.inFlight = new Set(); }
  onPartitionsAssigned(parts) { for (const p of parts) { const k = `${p.topic}:${p.partition}`; const start = (this.committedOffsets.get(k) ?? -1) + 1; this.seek(p.topic, p.partition, start); } }
  onPartitionsRevoked(parts) { const revoked = new Set(parts.map(p => `${p.topic}:${p.partition}`)); /* wait for inFlight on revoked before committing */ }
  processMessage(msg) { const id = `${msg.topic}:${msg.partition}:${msg.offset}`; this.inFlight.add(id); // downstream write then:
    this.inFlight.delete(id); const key = `${msg.topic}:${msg.partition}`; this.committedOffsets.set(key, msg.offset); }
  commitOffsets() { /* commit logic here */ }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of schema versioning, dead-letter routing, and offset discipline in KCNA.

## Key Concepts

- Versioned in-memory JSON schema registry
- Payload validation with a JSON schema validator
- Dead-letter routing to invalid_events
- Offset management and at-least-once semantics
- Lightweight deduplication for idempotence

## Code Example

```javascript
// Skeleton illustrating onMessage flow
function onMessage(msg) {
  const payload = JSON.parse(msg.value);
  const version = payload.schemaVersion;
  const schema = registry.get(msg.topic + '|' + version);
  if (!schema) { publishInvalid(msg, 'Unknown schemaVersion'); return; }
  if (!validate(payload, schema)) { publishInvalid(msg, 'Validation failed'); return; }
  publishMain(msg);
  commitOffsets(msg);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you evolve the registry for many topics? 
- How would you test canary scenarios, including missing schemas and duplicate messages?

Why This Is Asked
